CWE

CWE-1104 – Use of Unmaintained Third-Party Components

Description

During the assessment, the server was found to be running cURL version 7.29.0, which is an outdated release.

Older versions of cURL have been affected by numerous publicly disclosed security vulnerabilities, including issues related to certificate validation, protocol handling, memory safety, and HTTP request processing. While the presence of an outdated version alone does not confirm exploitability, it increases the likelihood that known vulnerabilities remain unpatched.

The installed version should be reviewed against vendor security advisories and updated to a supported release.

Evidence
$ curl --version

