libcurl/7.29.0
Impact

Running an outdated version of cURL may:

Expose the system to publicly disclosed vulnerabilities.
Increase the risk of exploitation if vulnerable features are enabled.
Result in non-compliance with organizational patch management requirements.
Reduce the overall security posture of the host.

The actual impact depends on the enabled protocols, compilation options, and the vendor's backported security patches.

Mitigation
Upgrade cURL to the latest vendor-supported version.
Apply all available operating system security updates.
Verify whether the Linux distribution has backported security fixes before determining exploitability.
Implement a regular vulnerability and patch management process for third-party software components.
